<title>USA: Goldman pays $100 mln for Commodities Corp - NYT.</title>
<headline>Goldman pays $100 mln for Commodities Corp - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co would pay about $100 million to acquire the Commodities Corp, an investment firm involved in managed futures, commodities and currencies, the New York Times said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Terms of the purchase were not disclosed but people familiar with the transaction said Goldman was paying $100 million to buy the Stockton Holdings Ltd unit, according to the newpaper. Both firms are privately-held.</p>
</text>
